# .trivyignore
#
# CVEs accepted for the published crowdsec-toolbox images, consumed by the
# Trivy scan in .github/workflows/release.yml. The scan already passes
# --ignore-unfixed, so every entry here is a finding that HAS a fix available
# and is accepted anyway. Each entry needs a reason and an `exp:` date, after
# which Trivy reports it again and forces a re-check.
#
# Format: `<id> exp:YYYY-MM-DD`, with the reason in a comment above it.

# pip vendors its own internal copy of msgpack for wheel metadata handling.
# This is not a dependency either tool declares or imports; it ships inside
# pip's own package (see pip/_vendor/msgpack) and is fixed only when pip
# itself updates that vendored copy upstream, independent of the pip version
# installed in the image.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 exp:2027-03-24

# setuptools ships an old vendored copy inside pip as well (pip/_vendor or
# its build backend chain), not as a package either tool installs or imports.
# Same upstream dependency as above: fixed when pip's own vendored copy is
# updated, not by anything in this repository's build.
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2027-03-24
